In this strategy, the designer should identify the weak points of the product in order to plan when, where and how a possible failure will occur. The weak points can be related to manufacturing, materials used and way of use. Usually, products have parts of different materials joined together, different materials have different failure point or wear (depending on mechanical or humans tractions and use). The failure can happen on three levels: system, process and product and for each level there different classification (minor, marginal, critical and catastrophic) and probability (extremely unlikely, remote, low to moderate, moderate and high) of failure occurrence.  

• Identify the effect of different fault for each part of the product;
• Identify the negative effect of failure in the user's eyes;
• Identification of group failure effect;
• Identify possible approaches for uncovering potential failures;
• Identify and forecast possible design changes to prevent or mitigate failure;